{"seconds": 36.7, "exit": 0, "final": "If Rd7+, Black just plays Kxd7 and is still up a rook. Perfect. The main line is: **Kc8 Rd8+ Kxd8 Rb8+ Kd7** and Black has won a whole rook with a completely winning position.\n\nThe motif here is a **quietMove** - moving the king to a seemingly passive square actually forces White's hand by positioning the king to attack both rooks.\n\n**Coaching Note:**\nWhen you're in check, don't just move your king to safety\u2014think actively. Kc8 looks passive, but it attacks both White rooks, forcing them to give checks. After Rd8+, you capture with Kxd8, winning a rook. The lesson: even when forced to move, look for moves that counter-attack and create threats.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Kc8\", \"line\": [\"Kc8\", \"Rd8+\", \"Kxd8\", \"Rb8+\", \"Kd7\"], \"motifs\": [\"quietMove\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "square": "d7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "square": "b7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "square": "c2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "square": "e8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "square": "c2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "move": "Ka8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1k2r3/1R1R4/8/5K2/8/5p2/PPr5/8 b - - 1 49", "move": "Kc8"}}, {"tool": "ch